-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",293,{
[9345]="7000875F\n1\tReturn to Taskmaster Gukthor at Dâr-gazag\030Collect food-sacks (total: 10)\tRations are portioned to enemy forces and found in locations where they hold power. Taskmaster Gukthor charged you collecting food for Angmar's Army.\n",
[9346]="70066069\n1\tCatch hearty fish (total: 4)\tBracha has asked you to catch fish in the Ringló. Catch fish north of the lumber camp near Ethring.\n2\tTalk to Bracha\tYou have caught several fish. Talk to Bracha at the lumber camp east of Ethring.\n",
[9347]="70068B63\n1\tRing the challenge bell to the south-east of Mêdi\tA challenge bell can be found to the south-east of Mêdi in the Lower Ward.\n2\tWait for your challenge to be answered\tYou have rung the challenge bell and should wait for your challenge to be answered.\n3\tRing the next challenge bell further to the south-east\tAnother challenge bell can be found further to the south-east in the Lower Ward.\n4\tWait for your challenge to be answered\tYou have rung the challenge bell and should wait for your challenge to be answered.\n5\tRing the last challenge bell to the north\tThe last challenge bell can be found to the north of the previous one, in the Lower Ward.\n6\tWait for your challenge to be answered\tYou have rung the challenge bell and should wait for your challenge to be answered.\n7\tTalk to Mûtahir by the last challenge bell\tMûtahir stands near the last challenge bell.\n8\tTalk to Mêdi in the Lower Ward\tMêdi is to the west of the last challenge bell, in the Lower Ward.\n",
[9348]="7003A45A\n1\tTalk to Baduhild\tBaduhild can be found in Mágla's home in central Middlemead. Thane Mágla has asked that you speak to his wife and son before bringing them to the Mead Hall. You should travel to Mágla's home.\n2\tCollect Mágla's sword\tMágla's sword can be found in his home in central Middlemead. Baduhild has asked you to bring Mágla's sword to her so that she might give it to her son to wield.\n3\tTalk to Séoca\tSéoca can be found in Mágla's home in central Middlemead. You have found Mágla's sword and should now present it to Séoca as Baduhild asked.\n4\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tThane Mágla can be found inside the Mead Hall of Middlemead in Kingstead. You have met with Mágla's family and should now return to him in the Mead Hall.\n5\tReady waggons for the people of Middlemead (total: 3)\tThe waggons can be found throughout Middlemead. Thane Mágla has asked you to ready the waggons as he bids his family and people farewell.\n6\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tThane Mágla can be found in the Mead Hall of Middlemead. You have readied the waggons for the people of Middlemead, and they now stand ready to journey to Edoras.\n",
[9349]="7001F3C0\n1\tFind and defeat Giltârk (quantity: see journal)\tMake your way north to the ruins in the northern Weather Hills and hunt down the leader of the Half-orcs and Orcs there. Aggie is concerned that she may have helped the half-orcs or Orcs in the ruins to the north and asked you for help in getting rid of her strange patron.\n2\tSpeak with Aggie Honeysuckle\tReturn to Aggie at the hunter camp near the bridge in the Midgewater Pass and tell her that you have defeated Giltârk. Aggie is at her encampment to the south of the ruins where you found Giltârk and the other Orcs and half-orcs.\n",
[9350]="7002C608\n1\tCollect spent arrows (total: 6)\030Collect spears (total: 6)\tSpears and arrows loosed in the battle can be found near the Orc battle-site in Thinglad. You should collect the fallen weapons for Wynmar to expedite the departure of his hunting party from Lórien territory.\n2\tBring the weapons to Wynmar\tWynmar is at his camp in the north-west of Thinglad. You should bring the weapons you collected to Wynmar.\n",
[9351]="7000F0BD\n1\tDefeat Great Winter-worm\t\n2\tSpeak to Weth in Zigilgund\tYou have made a dent in the population of worms around the dwarf-channels Weth described to you. You should return to him at Zigilgund.\n",
[9352]="70042C9A\n1\tGive Bingo's manuscript to Bilbo Baggins\tBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire, in Rivendell. Bingo has asked you to show the manuscript he has been writing to Bilbo Baggins, noted author and adventurer.\n2\tWait for Bilbo to finish reading Bingo's account of the journey\tBilbo is reading through Bingo's manuscript.\n3\tTalk to Bilbo Baggins in the Hall of Fire, and note his feedback for Bingo\tBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House. Bilbo has finished reading Bingo's manuscript, and is ready to give you his thoughts on it.\n4\tReturn the manuscript to Bingo and tell him what Bilbo thought of it\tBingo is in the Hall of Fire, in the Last Homely House.\n5\tDefeat dangerous creatures in the High Moor or Giant Valley (total: 10)\030Take some notes on the parchment at the Ford of Bruinen\tBingo has asked you to defeat dangerous creatures in the High Moors or Giant Valley, in the Trollshaws, and also to take notes on the parchment he gave you at the Ford of Bruinen.\n6\tReturn to Bingo in the Hall of Fire with your notes\tBingo is waiting in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House for you to return.\n7\tTalk to Bilbo Baggins in the Hall of Fire\tBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.\n8\tTalk to Bingo in the Hall of Fire\tBingo is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.\n",
[9353]="70030144\n1\tDefeat bats near the abandoned camp-site (total: 10)\tBats can be found around the abandoned encampment. You should defeat bats, for they do little but harass and annoy, and pose a threat to passers-by.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated several harassing, annoying bats in the centre of Fangorn's eaves.\n",
[9354]="70061441\n1\tDeliver Postman Grubb's letter to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving\tPostmaster Proudfoot can be found outside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. Postman Grubb has asked you to deliver a notice to Postmaster Proudfoot demanding an investigation into mail tampering and shortages in Yondershire.\n2\tFind Onyx Nethercot in the Quick Post in Michel Delving\tOnyx Nethercot can be found inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. Postmaster Proudfoot has asked you to find and speak to Onyx Nethercot, an associate postman, inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.\n3\tTalk to Onyx Nethercot in the Quick Post in Michel Delving\tOnyx Nethercot can be found inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. You have found Onyx Nethercot, an associate postman, at work inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. You should talk to Onyx Nethercot.\n4\tExamine the ledger in the Quick Post in Michel Delving\tThe ledger can be found on the counter inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. At Postmaster Proudfoot's request, Onyx Nethercot has produced the Quick Post's ledger for your perusal. You should examine the ledger and compare its records against those of Postman Grubb's account.\n5\tTalk to Onyx Nethercot in the Quick Post in Michel Delving\tOnyx Nethercot can be found inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. After examining the Quick Post's ledger, you have discovered a troubling discrepancy between Postman Grubb's account and the records of the Quick Post of Michel Delving. You should speak to Onyx Nethercot.\n6\tDeliver the ledger to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving\tPostmaster Proudfoot can be found outside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. After discovering a troubling discrepancy in the Quick Post's ledger, Onyx Nethercot has asked you to speak to Postmaster Proudfoot. You should speak to Postmaster Proudfoot.\n",
[9355]="70068349\n1\tDefeat Omkâru and collect its claw\tTevurin advised that a legendary ancient crab stalks the shores north and east of the expedition encampment. He asked that you help earn accolades by finding and defeating the creature.\n2\tDefeat Omkâru and collect its claw\tYou found the crab Tevurin spoke of and battled it to the death. You took its claw as a trophy and should return the claw to Tevurin at the hunter's expedition in the south-east of the Cape of Umbar as proof of your deed.\n",
[9356]="7000326B\n1\tBring Thoram's sword to Langlas\tLanglas is at the Thrasi's Lodge west of Kheledûl. Swayed by Toronn's reminder of their lost friend Thoram, Bregar asks you to bring the broken sword to Langlas, a Ranger of the North who will honour the sword and Thoram's memory.\n2\tBring the scroll to Bregar at Duillond\tBregar is at Duillond, along the road east and south of the Thrasi's Lodge. Langlas gratefully accepted Thoram's sword, promising to honour it, then gave you a scroll to deliver to Bregar.\n",
[9357]="700377CE\n1\tFind someone in Grimslade who might have information\tGrimslade is in the south-eastern reaches of the Westfold. You should search Grimslade for someone who may have had word of Grimbold, the Thane of Grimslade, or any of the other lords of the Mark who are missing.\n",
[9358]="7003FEAE\n1\tPlace bait on traps outside Alagrant (total: 8)\tTraps can be found outside Alagrant both east and west of the river Blackroot. Dírion has asked you to bait traps outside Alagrant so that he may get ahead on the day's hunting.\n2\tTalk to Dírion\tDírion can be found in Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale. You have placed bait on all of Dírion's traps and should now return to him.\n",
[9359]="70047BA8\n1\tEnter the Orc camp at Nuiharn\tAnborn has asked you to defeat the Orcs and their leader Bloglok camped in the ruins of Nuiharn. Nuiharn can be found in the hills to the north-west of Haerondir.\n2\tDefeat Orcs in Nuiharn (total: 12)\030Defeat Bloglok (quantity: see journal)\tAnborn has asked you to defeat the Orcs and their leader Bloglok camped in the ruins of Nuiharn. Nuiharn can be found in the hills to the north-west of Haerondir.\n3\tReturn to Anborn\tReturn to Anborn in Haerondir.\n",
[9360]="7006BF0B\n1\tApply Cúridwan's salve to copses afflicted with Lâg Dávrit (total: 9)\030Apply Cúridwan's salve to soil plots (total: 7)\tApply Cúridwan's salve to copses and soil plots afflicted with Lâg Dávrit in Vartúlin.\n2\tSpeak with Avadhril in Vartúlin\tSpeak with Avadhril in Vartúlin.\n",
[9361]="70028450\n1\tPlant seeds beneath ballistae (total: 5)\tThe ballistae can be found in the uruk-encampment of eastern Nan Curunír. Quickbeam asked you to plant seeds beneath the ballistae protecting the uruk-encampment.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam in Nan Curunír\tQuickbeam is at his home upon the north-eastern slopes of Nan Curunír. You should let Quickbeam know that the seeds have overgrown the uruks' siege-engines.\n",
[9362]="70048F7F\n1\tDefeat Nuzdum\tNuzdum can be found patrolling Mordor. You have encountered the threatening Nuzdum. Roaming the blasted rubble on the slopes of Udûn, the beast patrols the hillside with his pack.\n2\tDefeat Nuzdum\tNuzdum can be found patrolling The Wastes. You have encountered the threatening Nuzdum. Roaming the blasted rubble on the slopes of Udûn, the beast patrols the hillside with his pack.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Nuzdum.\n",
[9363]="70037BF0\n1\tDefeat Nágas\tNágas can be found among the perimeter outside of Brockbridge. Herefara has asked you to defeat the Uruk Nâgas, leader of the Brockbridge siege.\n2\tComplete\tThe overseer of the Brockbridge siege has been defeated, and those holding the siege will lack coordination for some time.\n",
[9364]="70022729\n1\tDefeat giants near the High Home (total: 5)\030Defeat giants near Mafân-mudun (total: 5)\tMafân-mudun is located in the south-eastern reaches of Thrór's Coomb, and the High Home may be found in the shadow of Harndirion to the south-east. Frithgeir has asked you to defeat giants at Mafân-mudun and the High Home.\n2\tTalk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund, north of Mafân-mudun and the High Home. You should return to Frithgeir and inform him that Nár's regards have been imparted upon the giants invading Thrór's Coomb.\n",
[9365]="7005A32F\n1\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in Erebor, the Lonely Mountain. Hersegg has offered to tell you Nár's tale as transcribed by her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. You should talk to Hersegg.\n2\tTalk to Hersegg at Akrâz-zahar\tHersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in Erebor, the Lonely Mountain. You have heard Hersegg's telling of Nár's tale as transcribed by her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. You should talk to Hersegg.\n",
[9366]="7001C69E\n1\tCollect Dhît's club\tNíels has asked you to seek out the troll Dhît in the western Trollshaws in the vicinity of the Stone-trolls' Glade and claim his club as proof of his death.\n2\tBring Dhît's club to Níels in Esteldín\tNíels is at Esteldín in the North Downs. You should bring Dhît's club to Níels.\n",
[9367]="7001C69A\n1\tCollect Farathlúg's scales\tNíels has asked you to seek out Farathlúg's cave along the northern edge of the Great Glacier in Forochel and collect his scales.\n2\tBring Farathlúg's scales to Níels in Esteldín\tNíels is at Estldín in the North Downs. You should bring Farathlúg's scales to Níels.\n",
[9368]="7001C69B\n1\tCollect Mangemaw's pelt\tNíels has asked you to seek out Mangemaw in Rushock Bog in the Shire and claim his pelt as proof of his death.\n2\tBring Mangemaw's pelt to Níels in Esteldín\tNíels is at Esteldín in the North Downs. You should bring Mangemaw's Pelt to Níels as proof of his death.\n",
[9369]="7001C69D\n1\tCollect Morrafn's crystal\tNíels has asked you to seek out Morrafn among the ruins in the western Fields of Fornost and banish the spirit beyond the Void.\n2\tBring Morrafn's crystal to Níels in Esteldin\tNíels is at Esteldín in the North Downs. You should bring Morrafn's crystal to Níels as proof of its defeat.\n",
[9370]="7001C69F\n1\tCollect Rothlúg's scales\tNíels has asked you to seek out Rothlúg atop the ridges of the southern Misty Mountains and claim his scales as proof of his defeat.\n2\tBring Rothlúg's scales to Níels in Esteldín\tNíels is at Esteldín in the North Downs. You should bring Rothlúg's scales to Níels as proof of his death.\n",
[9371]="70034D24\n1\tFind the beginning of the footprint trail\tA trail of very large footprints has been made through Gárnoth's Farm. They seem to originate from the north, near the road coming from Forlaw....\n2\tFind the beginning of the footprint trail\tThe path of footprints made by Núrzum start near the road from Forlaw toward Gárnoth's Farm. There appears to be a trail made by Núrzum recently. The footprints were made so deep they are still recognizable.\n3\tInvestigate the first footprint\tThe path of footprints made by Núrzum start near the road towards Gárnoth's Farm. There appears to be a trail made by Núrzum recently. The footprints were made so deep they are still recognizable.\n4\tInvestigate the second footprint\tThe path of footprints made by Núrzum continue to the east from the first one, found near the road toward Gárnoth's Farm. There appears to be a trail made by Núrzum recently. The footprints were made so deep they are still recognizable.\n5\tInvestigate the third footprint\tThe next in the path of footprints made by Núrzum is in the north-east corner of Gárnoth's Farm. There appears to be a trail made by Núrzum recently. The footprints were made so deep they are still recognizable.\n6\tInvestigate the fourth footprint\tThe final footprint made by Núrzum is near the centre of Gárnoth's Farm. There appears to be a trail made by Núrzum recently. The footprints were made so deep they are still recognizable.\n7\tCompleted\tNúrzum carved a path through Gárnoth's Farm to reach his Lieutenant on the southern side of the farm.\n",
[9372]="70034555\n1\tDefeat Orcs at the ice-spire\tOrcs can be found at one of the ice-spires marking a spot where Núrzum rested. You should defeat Orcs at the ice-spire.\n2\tDefeat Orcs at the ice-spire (total: 8)\tOrcs can be found at one of the ice-spires marking a spot where Núrzum rested. You should defeat Orcs at the ice-spire.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of Isengard's forces who settled into the shadow of Núrzum's presence. Wildermore is not yet safe, but the Orcs are not to call it home while its people still live.\n",
[9373]="70035C34\n1\tTalk to Barallas and witness Núrzum's wrath\tBarallas can be found at Stonecliff in northern Balewood. Barallas and the other Ents wish to tell you of the day Núrzum came to the Balewood.\n2\tTalk to Barallas\tBarallas can be found at Stonecliff in northern Balewood. Barallas' tale of Núrzum's arrival in the Balewood has ended. You should now speak with the Ent and discover what is to be done.\n",
[9374]="70007CC3\n1\tTalk to Sara Oakheart\tFollow Sara Oakheart out of Garth Agarwen and protect her along the way! She seems to have been captured by Ivar and the wights.\n2\tTell someone at the Eglain camp about Sara's rescue\tNow that you have successfully escorted Sara Oakheart to safety, you should speak with someone at the Eglan-camp.\n",
[9375]="7007162A\n1\tCollect Ahâba dates (total: 8)\030Collect oasis mulberries (total: 10)\030Collect citrus fruits (total: 8)\tBatâla has asked you to gather fruit from the trees and bushes in Ahâba. You should collect dates, mulberries, and citrus fruits around the oasis.\n2\tTalk to Batâla\tYou have collected fruit from the plants near the oasis. You should return to Batâla.\n",
[9376]="7004014D\n1\tSearch the Tingobel mine for the Dead\tThe mine can be found in Tingobel in north-eastern Blackroot Vale, to the north of Lancrath. Gúrion has asked you to search the Tingobel mine for signs of the Dead.\n2\tThe Dead can be found in the deepest reaches of the Tingobel mine. You have found a cold fire-pit in the depths of the Tingobel mine. Perhaps lighting the fire might draw the Dead forth.\t\n3\tTalk to Gúrion\tGúrion can be found along the northernmost roadway of Lancrath in south-eastern Blackroot Vale. You have temporarily quieted the Dead in the Tingobel mine. Before they vanished, they warned of a strange figure that attempted to gain their favour.\n",
})
